  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Annofoline may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular targets, with H9 being a common intermediate in all three pathways. Each of the three paths indicates that Annofoline targets H9, which in turn is a target of different compounds—Songorine, Betunolic Acid, and Communin B—each of which ultimately leads to Phosphodiesterase 6C. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.5067) suggest a potential functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports the possibility that Annofoline exerts its effects through H9, which may act as a bridge to Phosphodiesterase 6C, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction. The overlapping targets and similar scores imply a plausible biological pathway, but the precise role of H9 and the nature of the interactions between Annofoline and the other compounds remain areas for further investigation.",
